==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|punches out|punching out|punched out|punched out}}

# {{label|en|transitive}} To repeatedly hit a person
# {{label|en|transitive}} To hit so they become unconscious (knocked out)
#:{{usex|I'm going to '''punch out''' that [[SOB]] and leave him laying on the ground bleeding.|lang=en}}
# {{label|en|transitive}} To use a [[punch]] to remove a piece of material or to remove a piece already [[scored]].
#:{{usex|I spent all day '''punching out''' the die cut decals.|lang=en}}
# {{label|en|intransitive}} To leave a workplace by punching a [[timecard]]
#:{{usex|I'm going to '''punch out''' a bit early today.|lang=en}}
# {{label|en|intransitive}} To leave a workplace
# {{label|en|intransitive}} To eject from an airplane.
#:{{usex|With the engine on fire he had to '''punch out''' and hit the silk.|lang=en}}
# {{label|en|transitive|baseball}} To rule (by an [[umpire]]) that a pitch is a called third strike, often done emphatically.
#:{{usex|The ump '''punched out''' the batter with relish to close out the game.|lang=en}}
# {{label|en|transitive|baseball}} To throw a called third [[strike]].
#:{{usex|Jones '''punched out''' the batter to start in the sixth.|lang=en}}

====Antonyms====
{{sense|leave a workplace}} [[punch in]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|baseball|lang=en}} An instance of a called third strike.
#: ''Jones' '''punch out''' happened with the bases juiced.''

